Subject: [PATCH] Complete every manual Wasm save only after cache commit

Apply the cache destination policy in the existing shared save preflight,
including Save invoked by close/quit. An uploaded temporary file is not a
persistent destination even when it exists and is writable.

Gate the shared document completion on IDBFS acknowledgement before changing
metadata, clearing the dirty state or emitting save/download success. Keep
save/export callers waiting for that completion so failure cancels closing.
Autosave retains its separate completion path; desktop behavior is unchanged.
Commit manual bytes before deleting recovery data, and preserve an existing
layered snapshot across non-native saves until its synchronous native replacement is durable. Register recent URLs
after successful synchronous completion instead of queuing an already-fired signal.
User file dialogs select the browser cache; internal virtual destinations remain supported. Stage manual exports outside IDBFS; copy and restore targets inside the serialized
commit queue so a rejected save cannot be published by a later sync. Normalize
canonical browser paths for incremental saves.
Related desktop save-failure reports (not IDBFS):
https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=506760
https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=522480
For Wasm export staging, KRA and KRZ links use the logical filename, while
QML companion images use the physical output directory.
Commit every regular output produced by the exporter, not only the main file.
Upstream issue searches for browser staging, relative file-layer paths and
multi-file export commits found no matching report.

Set the native companion filter logical filename as well as its staged path.
Upstream searches for cache imports and companion KRA linked assets found no matching issue.

Reserve import recovery identity before probing its original source, keeping
relative assets intact without adopting the source's browser save identity.

Route Convert to File Layer through the bounded browser-cache file picker and
shared acknowledged exporter, so its referenced image outlives uploaded inputs.
Upstream searches found no corresponding WebAssembly persistence issue; inspected
related desktop conversion crash (not this cache defect):
https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=445831

Store configured backups beside the persistent output, so the acknowledged
primary commit includes the previous version. Use the same physical mapping
for incremental backups and validate/restore actual cached files in Open Recent.
Upstream searches found no matching WebAssembly backup/recent-file report.

Route welcome-page Recent clicks through the same cached-file opener as the
File menu. Remove missing entries only after persistent-file validation, not
when the user cancels named recovery. Upstream issue searches found no matching
WebAssembly cache-alias/recovery-cancellation report; the related welcome-page
preview crash https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=520362 has a different cause.

Synchronous exports to browser-cache destinations use the same staged output-set
commit and rollback as other manual exports. Layer export, Image Split and
Convert to File Layer therefore wait for persistence through one shared API.
Temporary resource and recovery exports keep their original synchronous path.
Upstream searches found no matching IndexedDB synchronous-export report.

Persist synchronous user exports by default, including new virtual paths from
Save Group Layers. Internal recovery, resource and template exports explicitly
remain temporary. Copied identical animation frames use the same acknowledged
output transaction as rendered frames. Upstream searches found no matching
WebAssembly persistence report.

Treat an uncached device input as a first save before incremental backup copies bytes. Ask for the persistent destination through the existing first-save branch, so the backup never belongs only to the upload directory. Internal incremental paths of already cached documents remain supported. Upstream issue searches found no matching WebAssembly upload-lifetime report.

Persist referenced uploaded file-layer inputs before native autosave, and in the same transaction as manual saves. Failed input persistence postpones autosave using its existing retry delay. Upstream issue searches found no matching WebAssembly upload/linked-recovery report.

Normalize complete logical file-layer paths before filesystem traversal on Wasm. Documents is an alias into IDBFS, so traversing its symlink before a following .. would incorrectly leave the logical root. Preserve persistent input aliases when releasing an upload group, including for another cached document still using them. Upstream issue searches found no matching WebAssembly logical-root report.

Keep uploaded file-layer identity in Wasm-only KRA metadata when closed browser sessions move saved documents. Retain ordinary sibling source names for desktop/device reopening. Upstream issue searches found no corresponding browser-session migration report; relative file-layer design is discussed in https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=413594.

Record the source session of persistent file layers in autosave snapshots so
closed-session imports remap their links without rewriting KRA archives or
opening a same-named file from the primary session. Relative file-layer design
is discussed in https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=413594; no matching
WebAssembly autosave import issue was found.

Make animation frame removal use the acknowledged browser cache transaction,
including the backing files of virtual outputs. No matching upstream
WebAssembly animation cleanup issue was found.

